 "notes": [],
 "working": "Let $P(x) = (x + 3)^6 (3x - 1)^5 = \\sum_{k=0}^{11} a_k x^k$.\n\nThe sum of the coefficients of the odd powers of $x$ is given by:\n$$S_{\\text{odd}} = a_1 + a_3 + a_5 + a_7 + a_9 + a_{11} = \\dfrac{P(1) - P(-1)}{2}$$\n\nStep 1: Evaluate $P(1)$:\n$$P(1) = (1 + 3)^6 (3(1) - 1)^5 = 4^6 \\cdot 2^5 = (2^2)^6 \\cdot 2^5 = 2^{12} \\cdot 2^5 = 2^{17}$$\n\nStep 2: Evaluate $P(-1)$:\n$$P(-1) = (-1 + 3)^6 (3(-1) - 1)^5 = 2^6 \\cdot (-4)^5 = 2^6 \\cdot (-(2^2)^5) = 2^6 \\cdot (-2^{10}) = -2^{16}$$\n\nStep 3: Compute $S_{\\text{odd}}$:\n$$S_{\\text{odd}} = \\dfrac{2^{17} - (-2^{16})}{2} = \\dfrac{2^{17} + 2^{16}}{2} = 2^{16} + 2^{15} = 2^{15}(2 + 1) = 3 \\cdot 2^{15}$$\n\nIndependent check: Sum of odd-power coefficients = [P(1) − P(−1)]/2. P(1) = 4^6·2^5 = 2^17 = 131072; P(−1) = 2^6·(−4)^5 = −2^16 = −65536. So sum = (131072 + 65536)/2 = 98304 = 3·2^15, verified by direct polynomial expansion.",
